condition_name: Panic Disorder
condition_slug: panic-disorder
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "A disorder characterized by episodic attacks of extreme fear, mostly unrelated to specific objects or situations. Associated with multiple somatic and cognitive symptoms. Each attack lasts for about 5 - 30 minutes. Often begins abruptly. Affects about 0.5 - 1.0% of the population"
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[9]: A feeling of choking,pounding heart,chest pressure or pain,dizziness,shortness of breath,trembling,sweating,tingling or numbness in the hands or feet,hot flushes
investigations[1]: As indicated to exclude medical aetiologies
treatment:
  goals[2]: Reduce intensity and frequency of attacks,Reduce anticipatory anxiety
  non_drug[1]: Cognitive-behavioural therapy
  drug[2]: "Fluoxetine: Adult: initially 20 mg orally once daily, increased after two weeks (if necessary) to 20 - 60 mg once daily (maximum 80 mg); Elderly: 20 - 40 mg (maximum 60 mg for elderly) once daily; Discontinue in both adults and elderly if no improvement within 10 weeks; Child and adolescent under 18 years: not recommended",Amitriptyline 50 - 150 mg orally/day
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[2]: Tricyclic antidepressants are cardio-toxic in overdose,Increased risk of suicidal attempts by patients with panic disorder
  supportive_measures[2]: Psychotherapy,Relaxation techniques
differential_diagnoses[3]: "Other causes of intense fear (phobias, obsessive-compulsive disorders, etc.)","Medical causes (e.g. hyperthyroid states, episodic hypoglycaemia, etc.)",Seizure disorders
complications[3]: Phobia,Depression,Suicide
prevention[1]: No specific primary prevention measures
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null